Let G = C_45 x C_7.  A group element [a,b] means residues a modulo 45 and b modulo 7; addition and negation are coordinatewise.
The base is an undirected multigraph on six vertices.  Each edge row chooses one displayed arrow as its positive dart; the reverse dart has the negative voltage.  A loop likewise has two opposite darts.
